================================================================================
Vendored quiche (`crates/leyline-quiche/`)
================================================================================

`leyline-quiche` is a fork of Cloudflare's `quiche` (v0.23.7) that links
against `leyline-bssl` instead of upstream `boring`, so Leyline's HTTP/2 and
HTTP/3 ClientHellos share the same patched BoringSSL.

Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/quiche
Copyright: Cloudflare, Inc.
License:   BSD-2-Clause — full text preserved at
           `crates/leyline-quiche/LICENSE` and `crates/leyline-quiche/COPYING`.

Modifications from upstream:
- Package renamed `quiche` -> `leyline-quiche`.
- `boring` / `tokio-boring` dependencies replaced with `leyline-bssl` /
  `leyline-bssl-tokio`.
- Bundled BoringSSL build (`boringssl-vendored` feature) removed — BoringSSL
  is provided by `leyline-bssl-sys` instead.

================================================================================
BoringSSL bindings (vendored under `crates/leyline-bssl*`)
================================================================================

TLS is provided by `leyline-bssl`, `leyline-bssl-sys`, and `leyline-bssl-tokio`,
vendored in-tree as a fork of 0x676e67's `btls` (itself a fork of `boring2`).
They fork Cloudflare's `boring` crate and Google's BoringSSL C library, pin the
BoringSSL revision per Chrome era, and add the fingerprint-critical extensions
Leyline requires:

- `SSL_CTX_set_record_size_limit` (RFC 8449) — Firefox profiles.
- `SSL_CTX_set_delegated_credentials` (RFC 9345) — Firefox profiles.
- MLKEM768 / post-quantum key agreement codepoints.
- Deterministic GREASE ordering and ClientHello extension permutation hooks.

Upstream: https://github.com/0x676e67/btls
Licenses: the Rust bindings are Apache-2.0 / MIT. The bundled BoringSSL C
          library is Apache-2.0 (relicensed by Google), with a BSD-3-Clause
          notice for Go-derived test tooling that is not linked into the
          shipped libraries.

================================================================================
BoringSSL binary provenance (prebuilt static libraries)
================================================================================

`leyline-bssl-sys` ships prebuilt BoringSSL static libraries under
`crates/leyline-bssl-sys/native/<target>/lib/` ({libcrypto,libssl}.a / {crypto,ssl}.lib)
for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, x86_64-pc-windows-msvc,
and aarch64-apple-darwin.
These are statically linked into every distributed binary artifact — the Node
N-API addon (`.node`) and the Python wheel. Their full license text (Apache-2.0
plus the BSD-3-Clause Go notice) is preserved at
`crates/leyline-bssl-sys/LICENSE-BORINGSSL`, and the MIT binding-glue grant at
`crates/leyline-bssl-sys/LICENSE-MIT`. The npm packages and Python wheels carry a
`LICENSE` conveying these obligations; the source distribution (sdist) builds
BoringSSL from source instead and does not redistribute these binaries.

